WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.230
I was chasing him, the poor soul who saw me.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:09.580
He was wearing a thick, red winter coat and
glasses, climbing up the side of the mountain

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.510
with a sharp little tool.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:14.540
If I had known he was coming, I would have
run.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:15.960
Of course, I would have run.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.660
But it was already too late.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:23.660
The second he saw me, saw my horrible, ugly
face, it was already over.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.960
I felt all those familiar feelings bubble
up.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.580
I knew, as well as I knew anything in life,
that I would need to kill him.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:32.580
My name...

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.050
Well, I don’t know my name.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.050
Not really.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.399
I think I had one once, a long, long time
ago.

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:44.840
I don’t think I always looked like this
- like this big, ugly monster.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.130
But who can say?

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:49.250
Those memories were blown away like a snowdrift.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:53.100
Life - this life, at least - has never been
easy for me.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.219
I don’t like hurting people.

00:00:55.219 --> 00:00:59.440
But at least, up there in the mountains, people
didn’t see me that often.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:02.670
How could I know about the strange men who
would come for me?

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:06.780
How could I possibly know that it was all
going to get so much worse?

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.931
The poor man in the red coat who saw me tried
his best to run.

00:01:10.931 --> 00:01:13.280
I think my crying frightened him.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:18.820
I wish my mouth could make words - If it could,
I would have told him how sorry I was.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:20.510
But it didn’t matter anymore.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:25.860
I kept moving towards him, like I was being
pulled along by some invisible leash in his

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:26.860
direction.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.100
I tried to stop.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.960
I tried to think really hard, to focus.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.860
I kept telling myself, “No, not this time.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.869
You’re better than this.

00:01:34.869 --> 00:01:36.140
You can let this one go.”

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:42.430
But before the sentence is even fully formed
in my mind, I’m already on top of him.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:46.750
I look down and see his terrified face, tears
frozen on his cheeks.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:51.740
Eyes wide with horror you can’t even begin
to describe - If you haven’t seen my face.

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:53.750
He was still looking at me.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.610
It hurt that he was looking at me.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:00.110
I leaned in and opened my mouth, wide enough
to swallow him whole.

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:05.640
Soon enough, there was nothing left of the
man in the red coat, and I was alone again.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:10.140
All I could think to do was sit there on the
freezing mountainside and weep.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.730
Why did I keep doing this?

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.540
Why couldn’t I stop myself?

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:19.010
I’d asked myself these questions again and
again, but I never got an answer.

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:22.830
It felt like I knew myself a little less every
single day.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:28.800
Sometime later - I don’t know how many days,
weeks, or months - two huge, black, noisy

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:32.020
creatures came towards me out of the sky.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.940
The second I saw them, I turned and started
moving away.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.140
I couldn’t let those creatures see me.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.540
I knew something terrible would happen if
they did.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:43.610
It was best just to move away, let them leave
me alone.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:44.610
Nobody had to die.

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:48.720
What I didn’t know was that I was the reason
they were there.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:53.560
The two flying black creatures landed on the
mountain behind me, and groups of people climbed

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:56.569
out, carrying strange objects I didn’t recognize.

00:02:56.569 --> 00:03:01.360
I huddled myself away in a corner as one of
the men came towards me.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.180
I was so afraid I couldn’t stop myself from
crying.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:08.940
I didn’t have the words - I couldn’t tell
them how much danger they were in.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:13.299
Couldn’t tell them that I didn’t want
to hurt them, that they should just leave

00:03:13.299 --> 00:03:14.299
me here.

00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:15.890
But it was already too late.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:19.409
One of the strange men walked right in front
of me, and saw my face.

00:03:19.409 --> 00:03:22.019
He said, “Jesus, this thing is one ugly—“

00:03:22.019 --> 00:03:23.810
I started screaming.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.489
I couldn’t stop myself.

00:03:25.489 --> 00:03:27.890
My head started going fuzzy and my heart hurt.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:34.319
The man who’d seen my face was already backing
away, knowing just a few seconds too late

00:03:34.319 --> 00:03:36.500
that he’d made an awful mistake.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.390
It wouldn’t save him now.

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:39.750
Nothing could save him.

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:42.940
I tried to stop myself, but trying hurt.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:45.190
It just made me scream louder.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:49.910
I turned and lunged at him, but that made
things worse: Now, so many of the others had

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:51.299
seen my face, too.

00:03:51.299 --> 00:03:56.530
With fat, wet tears rolling down my cheeks,
I knew that I would have to destroy them all

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.900
- even though I didn’t want to.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:03:59.900
But this time, they fought back.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:06.500
I suddenly heard all these horrible loud noises
all around me, and felt white-hot pain all

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:07.500
over my body.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.480
They were shooting at me, both with the objects
they held, and other, even larger weapons

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.780
attached to their strange, flying vehicles.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:18.670
This made my confusion and anger even worse.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:22.810
I went berserk, jumping at them and attacking
them with my claws and teeth.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:27.570
They may have been able to hurt me more than
ordinary people, but they were just as easy

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.760
to destroy as anyone.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:35.100
Not that it made me feel any less terrible
for doing it, even though they attacked me

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.100
first.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.530
Who were these strange, aggressive people?

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:40.830
And why had they come here to attack me?

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:43.630
Soon enough, I’d destroyed all the ones
who had seen my face.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:47.050
There was nothing left to do but just sit
there and weep again.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:50.950
I felt so terrible about everything I’d
done to them.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:53.940
It was a pain deep, deep in my chest.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:59.410
But then, suddenly, everything went black,
and a sack was pulled over my head.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:01.960
I couldn’t see who did it, and I’m glad
I didn’t.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.380
More importantly, they didn’t see me.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:08.440
I think after that, they bundled me onto one
of their flying vehicles and took me away.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:11.440
I had no idea where I’d end up next.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:15.839
All I could do was stand there with a bag
over my head, and cry.

00:05:15.839 --> 00:05:19.540
Still blinded, and after a long period of
flying through the air, I was pulled out of

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.340
the vehicle and dragged away somewhere.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.530
I felt grateful that I didn’t know.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:26.660
If I was here to be punished, it was probably
what I deserved.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:31.620
Soon enough, I was brought into a room where
a bunch of strangers were looking at me.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:35.330
I’d later learn that one of these strangers
was called Dr. Dan.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:40.290
And Dr. Dan seemed very interested in what
had happened back on the mountain.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:43.270
The one who put the bag over my head was talking
to Dr. Dan.

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:46.039
He said, “That thing killed all of my men.

00:05:46.039 --> 00:05:48.009
Tore through them like tissue paper.

00:05:48.009 --> 00:05:52.319
Our heavy artillery barely slowed it down,
and it regenerated any damage it sustained

00:05:52.319 --> 00:05:53.319
almost immediately.”

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:55.810
“Fascinating,” Dr. Dan said.

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:59.050
“And yet it seems so docile now.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:00.169
Why?

00:06:00.169 --> 00:06:03.449
What activated its rage state during the confrontation?”

00:06:03.449 --> 00:06:04.880
“Connors looked at its face.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.729
That’s when it went ballistic.”

00:06:06.729 --> 00:06:09.789
Hearing the story told again, I started to
weep.

00:06:09.789 --> 00:06:13.360
It was true; everything they were saying was
true.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:17.190
I killed all those poor people, even though
I couldn’t help it.

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:21.310
There was no place for me in this world, if
all I could do was hurt people.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:24.470
I’d be better off not existing at all.

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:26.980
Everything was a bit of a blur after that.

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:30.220
The next time the bag was removed, I was in
some kind of room.

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:35.250
A perfect cube that clanked and clunked every
time I moved around it.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.940
No windows, no doors.

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:39.530
Probably for the best.

00:06:39.530 --> 00:06:44.750
All I could do was pace around this little
cube and wait, wait until Dr. Dan was ready

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.699
to conduct more of his tests.

00:06:46.699 --> 00:06:52.350
I’d never felt more empty and alone, but
at least I couldn’t hurt anyone here.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:54.800
Thank heavens for small mercies.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:57.850
Sometime later, I was bagged again and taken
out of the cube.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:03.250
I don’t know where they took me, but suddenly,
I felt that terrible feeling again.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:07.530
Knowing that someone out there had seen my
awful, ugly face.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:11.009
Knowing that, no matter what I really wanted
to do, I had to destroy them.

00:07:11.009 --> 00:07:12.710
It was the only way.

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:15.400
But how had they even seen my face while I
was wearing the bag?

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:16.970
It didn’t make sense.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:18.560
None of it made any sense.

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:21.960
I felt the strong tug of the invisible leash
again.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.130
Pulling me towards the one who’d seen me.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:28.960
I screamed and roared and waited and tore
off the bag.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:33.350
I started galloping across the land in front
of me, all barren and empty, until I reached

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:34.350
the water.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.090
I was right next to the ocean.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:38.340
I leaped in and started diving.

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:41.569
Getting deeper, deeper, deeper.

00:07:41.569 --> 00:07:44.650
Eventually, I found a strange metal sphere.

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:49.710
Somehow, I just knew the one who had seen
my face was somewhere in there.

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:53.840
I tore it open and found him, a man in an
orange jumpsuit.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:56.120
He screamed as water filled his lungs.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.230
Moments later, he was gone.

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:03.210
I swam back to shore, tears dissolving in
the ocean, where the strange men bagged me

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:05.500
again, and I was back in the cube.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:07.130
It was a moment of calm.

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:09.780
Soon, things were going to get so much worse.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:13.080
That terrible day, it happened a lot like
last time.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:14.800
The time next to the ocean.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:20.340
I was inside my cube when I felt that terrible
feeling, the sensation of being looked at.

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:24.970
This time, I somehow sensed that the one who
saw me was even further away.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:27.280
I said to myself, this time, I’d resist.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:28.879
I’d stop myself.

00:08:28.879 --> 00:08:30.040
Nobody would be hurt.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:33.289
But resisting the pull hurt me even more.

00:08:33.289 --> 00:08:38.140
All I could do was wait and howl in terrible
pain, as I heard people panicking and scrambling

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:40.229
outside the walls of my room.

00:08:40.229 --> 00:08:42.149
Soon enough, it was too late.

00:08:42.149 --> 00:08:44.200
I couldn’t stop myself.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:47.410
I needed to find the one who saw me and destroy
them.

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:51.220
The walls gave way like wet sand as I tore
through them.

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:55.971
There were so many people in white coats standing
around the room.

00:08:55.971 --> 00:09:00.200
A terrible-smelling gas that burned my throat
flooded the room, killing most of the people

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.200
around me.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:06.959
But as always, I survived, and I started running,
feeling the pull towards the person who saw

00:09:06.959 --> 00:09:07.959
my face.

00:09:07.959 --> 00:09:13.380
I busted through walls and galloped across
the ground, feeling the miles tick by each

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:14.380
second.

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:18.521
I could hear the distant hum of more of those
flying vehicles in the air behind me, but

00:09:18.521 --> 00:09:19.839
it didn’t matter.

00:09:19.839 --> 00:09:21.140
None of it mattered.

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:25.420
All that mattered was finding the one who
saw me and wiping them off the face of the

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:28.130
earth, no matter how awful it made me feel
inside.

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:32.839
Soon, I arrived at a town where everyone was
gathered in the center.

00:09:32.839 --> 00:09:37.529
They all turned and looked at me, and I could
feel the rage rising to a fever pitch.

00:09:37.529 --> 00:09:41.560
There were so many of them, all those poor
people.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:46.329
And not long after, more people with guns
arrived, wearing strangle goggles.

00:09:46.329 --> 00:09:48.220
They all looked at my face too.

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:49.649
I couldn’t help it.

00:09:49.649 --> 00:09:50.720
I’m so sorry.

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.710
I just couldn’t help it.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:57.630
I try not to think about how many people I
killed that day, but soon enough, a bag was

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:02.970
placed back over my head, and I was dragged
back to my room - which they’d rebuilt while

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:03.970
I was gone.

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:11.160
I remained in there for a long time, just
weeping, consumed by my own seemingly endless

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:12.310
sadness.

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:18.209
Until one day, sometime later, I was dragged
out of my room and taken to another chamber.

00:10:18.209 --> 00:10:22.481
I could hear something that wasn’t human
breathing when they pulled the bag off of

00:10:22.481 --> 00:10:23.481
my head.

00:10:23.481 --> 00:10:27.200
I was standing across from a monster, staring
right at my face.

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:32.060
A huge, terrible reptile, with a thick hide
and giant claws and teeth.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:34.100
It hissed when it saw me.

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:35.640
It was happening again.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:39.040
The pain started; I was weeping and wailing.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:40.709
Was this all my life would ever be?

00:10:40.709 --> 00:10:43.720
A mix of silence and violence?

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:49.750
Only existing to hurt others and be sad, hurt,
and alone, unable to even control my own actions?

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:52.070
What kind of a life is that, if you can even
call it a life?

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:57.510
The monster hissed and said, “You are disgussssting.”

00:10:57.510 --> 00:11:00.070
Silently, I agreed.

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:07.970
Now go check out “SCP-096 - The Shy Guy”
and “SCP-096 VS SCP-343” for more tragic

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:09.580
tales of the Shy Guy!

